    "text": "The combustion of benzene <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></math> gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math> Given that heat of combustion of benzene at constant volume is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3263</mn><mo>.9</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>;</mo></math>&nbsp;the heat of combustion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>in</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>kJ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> of benzene at constant pressure will be<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.314</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"
